.TH CANNELIA-CAPTURE 1 "October 2026" "Cannelia Capture" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cannelia-capture \- capture screens, windows and regions on Cinnamon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cannelia-capture
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Capture screenshots with automatic saving, clipboard integration and an
interactive editor. Linux Mint with Cinnamon on X11 is the validated environment.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-interactive
Open the graphical interface.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-area
Select a rectangular region.
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-window
Capture the active window.
.TP
.B \-\-select-window
Pick a window interactively, when supported by the compositor.
.TP
.BI \-\-monitor " INDEX"
Capture a monitor by zero-based index.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-clipboard
Send the capture directly to the clipboard.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-include-pointer
Include the mouse pointer, when supported.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-include-shadow
Include the window shadow, when supported.
.TP
.BI \-\-delay " SECONDS"
Wait before capturing.
.TP
.BI \-\-file " PATH"
Save to the specified path.
.TP
.B \-\-check
Check the backend and dependencies without capturing.
.TP
.B \-\-profile
Print elapsed save time as JSON on standard error.
.TP
.B \-\-no-notification
Disable desktop notifications.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the product name and version.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print all command-line options.
.SH FILES
Preferences are stored in the cinnamon-screenshot-local directory beneath
XDG_CONFIG_HOME (by default ~/.config). Captures default to the user's Pictures
folder. Use the Preferences dialog to change the destination and capture options.
